{"text": "00\n\nContract Research\nTelephone +49-2203-303-1\n\nTelefax +#49-2203-305.362\nINBIFO GmbH - Fuggerstr. 3- 51149 Cologne + Germany\nTo: Loreen McAlpin Fax No: 001-804.274-3082\nManager, WSA Programs\nand Planning\nPhilip Mortis Richmond\nFrom: Wolf Reininghaus Date: 5.0ct.2000\nTotal Number of Pages: 14 Telefax Message No.:\nURGENT OFOR REVIEW PLEASE COMMENT PLEASE REPLY\n\nRe: Rick's request for anti-tobacco publishers\n\nDear Loreen,\nPlease find attached a published discussion on the anti-tobacco position of 2 American\njoumals. We assume that the New England Journal of Medicine has a similar negative\nposition, For me the pro and con arguments look quite helpful.\n\n| also include the letters we exchanged with Cancer Research which show that they act\n\u201cunfriendly\u201d without giving clear reasons.\n\n| believe Rick's initiative is helpful and necessary.\nTo my knowledge there are, except some academic organizations in England, none who\ndon't accept tobacco funding in some way or the other (I'm not sure about the position of\n\nthe DKFZ in Germany). That, however, does not mean that funding will not be resented\nand fought by pressure groups.\n\nBest regards,\n\nwot retinas\n\npzzesoesoe\n\nRAPAMGALP AUTE-TORACCO.BOE \u201cTote Regier cago MR 267\n\u2018Sonera tanger be Wot Rerahaue -\n\noanyast zeccoe cozz ert IVA GO:ZT OG 00. oT/S0",
